      "description": "Open Positions - Human Resources - University of Dallas Skip to main content Toggle menu UD Police News Events Library My UD Academics Academics Overview Program Finder Bulletin & Course Catalog Colleges & Schools The Rome Experience Faculty The Neuhoff Institute Centers & Institutes Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Overview Undergraduate Admissions & Aid Graduate Admissions & Aid Ministry Admissions Financial Aid Visit UD Contact Admissions Life at UD Life at UD Overview Student Clubs & Organizations Housing & Dining Health & Wellness Campus Ministry Office of Student Life Office of Personal Career Development Academic Success Library Bookstore Faith & Service Faith & Service Overview Our Catholic Faith Serving Others Serving the Church Church of the Incarnation Athletics About UD About the University Academic Excellence UD At a Glance Dallas/Fort Worth Area Leadership Mission & Vision Offices & Services INFO FOR Alumni Donors Parents & Families Visitors The Core is an opportunity to inquire into the fundamental aspects of being and our\n               relationship with God, nature and our fellow human beings. Explore the Core Toggle search search Search Popular Searches Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Core Curriculum Library Financial Aid University of Dallas University of Dallas Apply Request Info Visit Give Open Positions Home - Offices & Services - Human Resources - Open Positions Human Resources Human Resources HR Staff Open Positions Benefits to Eligible Employees Dental and Vision Insurance Benefits Eligibility Employee Assistance Program Family Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Life and Long-Term Disability Insurance Medical Insurance Retirement Tuition Exchange Program Employee Tuition Waiver Worker's Compensation Accommodation Services HR Forms & Resources Student Employment Open Positions Employment Opportunities Open Faculty Positions Part Time Please note that the part time positions below are open on a continuous basis so when\n                                             a part time faculty is needed there is a pool of candidates available to choose from. Adjunct Instructor, Various Courses, Constantin College and Braniff Graduate School\n                                                of Liberal Arts Adjunct Instructor, Various Courses, Gupta College of Business Refer to individual job postings for specific application procedures. Full Time We currently do not have any full-time faculty opportunities, please check again later. Open Staff Positions Part Time We currently do not have any part-time opportunities, please check again later. Full Time Administrative Assistant - Mathematics and Physics Admission Counselor Baseball Coach Career Advisor Content Marketing Manager Development Project Manager Financial Assistant Note on Employment Eligibility All offers, including those for faculty, are contingent upon favorable background\n                              and reference checks, as well as submission of the required documentation of right\n                              to work. EEO Statement The University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and\n                              administration of the highest caliber. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and encourages applications from\n                              individuals who will enhance our community and advance our Mission. Affirmative Action Plan The University of Dallas embraces the call for advancing human dignity in work, and\n                              has elected to engage in a program of affirmative action in its pursuit. Affirmative\n                              action is defined by federal legislation and executive order, and for which the university\n                              through its standing as a federal grantee is subject to its requirements. The University\n                              is committed to the attraction and advancement of women, minorities, veterans and\n                              qualified individuals with disabilities through a systematic program of recruiting,\n                              development, and pay equity. Employees and applicants who would like to request a\n                              viewing of the University's Affirmative Action Plan should submit a request in writing\n                              to hrdept@udallas.edu . Keep Exploring Discover the University of Dallas Cost and Aid Core Curriculum University of Dallas Apply Request Info Visit Give 1845 East Northgate Drive Irving, Texas 75062-4736 (972) 721-5000 DIRECTIONS CONTACT US Accessibility Services Bookstore Campus Map Compliance Reporting Hotline Consumer Information Directory Employment Events Library News Offices & Services Online Disclosure Statement Title IX & Sexual Violence Thoughts from the Tower Blog UD Police University Policies © 2026 University of Dallas LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube Podcasts ©"
