    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Adjunct%20Faculty_Constantin-Braniff_11.2025.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor                                            Job Number: 2161UD",
      "description": " \n \n Adjunct Instructor                                            Job Number: 2161UD  \nConstantin College and Braniff Graduate School of Liberal Arts  \n  \nSUMMARY \n \nAdjunct faculty to teach courses in the academic departments of Art, Biology, Chemistry, Classics, Drama, \nEconomics, Education, English, History, Math, Modern Languages, Philosophy, Physics, Politics, \nPsychology, and Theology.  \n \nWe are particularly seeking to hire faculty to teach in the following areas. The courses listed under a \ngiven area will likely be in particular need of faculty. \n \nBiology \n• Laboratory courses in Anatomy \n• Laboratory courses in Physiology \n• Laboratory courses in Microbiology \n \nChemistry \n• Organic Chemistry I and II \n• Laboratory courses in Organic Chemistry \n \nClassics \n• First- or second-year courses in Latin \n• First- or second-year courses in Greek \n \nEnglish \n• ENG 1301: Literary Tradition I \n• ENG 1302: Literary Tradition II \n \nHistory \n• HIS 1312 American Civilization II \n• HIS 2302 Western Civilization II \n \nMath \n• MAT 1303 Precalculus \n \nPhysics \n• General Physics I and II \n• Laboratory courses in General Physics  \n \nPolitics \n• POL 1311: Principles of American Politics  \n \n \n \nSpanish \n• MSP 1301 First Year Spanish I \n• MSP 1302 First Year Spanish II \n• MSP 2311 Second Year Spanish I \n \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES \n \n• Instruct undergraduate and/or graduate students. \n• Invite, facilitate, and moderate classroom discussion. \n• Evaluate and grade student coursework. \n• Maintain student attendance records, grades, and other required records. \n• Communicate with students to provide necessary guidance and assistance. \n• Participate in meetings pertinent to faculty responsibilities. \n \n \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS \n \n• Master’s degree with at least 18 graduate credit hours in teaching area (for teaching \nundergraduate-level courses). \n• Earned doctorate degree in disciplinary field (for teaching graduate-level courses). \n \n \nWHO WE ARE \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \n \nAPPLICATION \n \nAll applications should be submitted online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/  \n   \n \n  \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \n \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Adjunct%20Faculty_COB_09.2025.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor                                        Job Number: 000027UD",
      "description": " \n  \n  \nAdjunct Instructor                                        Job Number: 000027UD  \nGupta College of Business  \n  \n \nWHO WE ARE \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \nSUMMARY  \n  \nThe University of Dallas’ Gupta College of Business is seeking dynamic adjunct faculty members to \ninstruct assigned undergraduate and/or graduate business courses. We are especially interested in \nprofessionals who are actively working in their fields and eager to bring current industry knowledge, \npractices, and insights into the classroom. Course areas may include: Accounting, Business Analytics, \nBusiness Communications, Business, Ethics, Business law, Business Mathematics & Statistics, \nCybersecurity, Economics, Entrepreneurship, Finance, Global Business, Information Technology \nManagement, Marketing, Management, Operations, Writing Academic Tutor, Finance Academic Tutor, \nand Statistics Academic Tutor.  \n  \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES   \n \n• Prepare and deliver lectures that integrate academic content with real-world, industry-based \napplications. \n• Draw from current professional experiences to facilitate and enrich classroom discussions. \n• Evaluate and grade student coursework in alignment with academic standards. \n• Maintain student attendance records, grades, and other required documentation. \n• Plan, evaluate, and revise course content, materials, and instructional methods to ensure both \nacademic rigor and industry relevance. \n• Maintain regularly scheduled office hours to advise and mentor students. \n• Communicate proactively with students to provide guidance and support. \n• Stay current in both your professional field and in teaching practices through continuous \ndevelopment and engagement. \n• Participate in meetings and collaborative efforts that support the mission of the Gupta College of \nBusiness. \n \n  \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS   \n• Master’s degree from an AACSB-accredited institution (or comparable accreditation specific to the \nfield) with at least 18 graduate credit hours in the teaching area. \n• Significant professional experience in a business-related field, with the ability to integrate industry \nexpertise into teaching.  \n• Experience teaching business-related courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level.  \n• Excellent oral and written communication skills.  \n• Strong presentation skills and a clear focus on the discipline.  \n• Significant business management skills.  \n• Knowledge and practice of a variety of instructional methods and technology that ensure successful \nstudent learning. Experience with experimental learning.  \n• Ability to work well in a collaborative work environment.  \n• Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and student success.  \n  \n PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS  \n• Currently employed in a business, finance, technology, or management role that directly relates \nto course content. \n• Teaching experience in either online or face to face format.  \n  \n \nAPPLICATION \nAll applications should be submitted online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/  \n  \n  \n  \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \n \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. \n "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Administrative%20Assistant_Math%20and%20Physics_08.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant- Mathematics and Physics",
      "description": " \n \n                                                                                      Job Number: 17078UD \n          Date Posted: September 2, 2026 \nAdministrative Assistant- Mathematics and Physics                                             \n \nWHO WE ARE  \n \nThe University of Dallas is a Catholic university that seeks to educate the whole person, \nencouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and primary ends of \neducation. We have consistently ranked as one of the top regional universities in the country. \nWe are dedicated and guided by our Mission. \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking a part-time Administrative Assistant to provide support for the \nMathematics and Physics departments’ routine business and academic activities. This position \nalso provides administrative support for the Journalism program as needed.   \n \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES  \n \n• Answer phone calls and direct calls to appropriate offices or take messages.  \n• Assist with managing faculty calendars: schedules, conferences, and travel. \n• Manage department calendar and email account for all official department events \nand communication. \n• Coordinate the maintenance and repair of office equipment. Maintain supply \ninventory. \n• Sort and route incoming correspondence, including mail. Prepare outgoing mail.  \n• Perform data entry and prepare reports, letters, and spreadsheets, and other \ndocuments, including EAFs, student EPAFs, using work processing and database \nforms and software.  \n• Schedule student clerical and/or lab workers’ assignments.  \n• Maintain course files, including files or class materials and course evaluations.  \n• Assist in maintaining records including loading course evaluations and other records \non shared departmental drives. \n• File and retrieve documents, records, reports, and other materials.  \n• Assist the department chairs in tracking faculty course loads.  \n• Assist in maintaining the department website in coordination with the department \nwebmaster. \n• Help with department newsletters and communication with alumni and prospective \nstudents. \n \n• Monitor and reconcile budget to track expenditures using the FAST system. \n• Hire student workers and manage their work so that classrooms and laboratory \nspaces are well maintained.  \n• Plan and oversee receptions for departmental events.  \n• Assist the Director of the Journalism program on an ad hoc basis with any \nadministrative needs.  \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS  \n• High school diploma/GED. \n• Previous office administration experience.  \n• Ability to communicate effectively and grammatically, both orally and in writing.  \n• Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with individuals throughout \nthe University.  \n• High degree of flexibility.  \n• Ability to maintain emotional control under stress. \n• Ability to take initiative to identify problems and find solutions to address departmental \nneeds. \n• Strong computer skills, including ability to work with Word, Excel, Google Workspace, \nBanner, and FAST.  \n• Capable of being able to track progress in long, ongoing, overlapping projects. \n• Proficiency in accounting/bookkeeping. \n \nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS \n \n• Some college work. \n \nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n \n• This is a part-time, 20 hour per week position.  \n \nBENEFITS  \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions.   \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Admission%20Counselor_08.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "students/ parents, and contact students and parents via phone, email and mail. This position",
      "description": " \n \n                                                                                      Job Number: 16699UD \nAdmission Counselor                                                         Date Posted: August 24, 2026 \n \nWHO WE ARE  \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking an Admission Counselor to recruit qualified students for admission and \nenrollment to the University of Dallas within assigned territory. The Admission Counselor will \ntravel to off-campus recruitment events, evaluate application files for admission decisions, \nmeet with students in person, conduct on-campus admission presentations to groups of \nstudents/ parents, and contact students and parents via phone, email and mail. This position \nwill communicate effectively on the value of a UD education, the technical nature of the \nfinancial aid process, the merits of specific majors and concentrations, and the traditions that \nhelp build UD’s unique community. \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES  \n \n• Nurture, build, and sustain ongoing professional relationships with prospective students \nand those who influence them to achieve assigned enrollment management objectives. \n• Become familiar with the college admission process, including but not limited to sources \nof students, preferences of students, and sources of competition. Learn and use what \nworks best for achievement of enrollment management objectives.  \n• Research the potential for travel and recruiting programs, develop a plan for off-campus \nactivities to achieve enrollment management objectives most effectively, present this \nplan for the Director’s approval, and then execute the approved plan within the \napproved budget. \n• Cultivate alumni, parents, college counselors, and other constituencies to assist with the \nrecruitment process. \n• Monitor the inquiry, prospect, application, and deposit numbers to focus on attaining \nassigned objectives. \n• Determine the best next source and means of institutional contact for prospects. \n \n• Re-qualify the inquiry pool, so that those inquiries most likely to enroll are the ones \nbeing contacted on a regular basis. \n• Monitor the receipt of applications and determine the best next steps in the \nrecruitment process for each applicant. \n• Ensure that all inbound and outbound communication with prospects and applicants is \nrecorded using office protocol. \n• Evaluate applications for admission and make each admit/deny decision using \ndiscretionary professional judgment about the applicant’s academic preparation, \nacademic work ethic, and fit for the academic programs at the University of Dallas. \n• Document activity and decisions about applications for admission in accordance with \nestablished standards. \n• Communicate with prospective students about financial aid, financial resources, and \nhow to pay for college. \n• Other duties as assigned to ensure the efficient and effective operation of the Office of \nUndergraduate Admission. \n \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS  \n• Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university. \n \nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n \n• Supervise, train, mentor, and evaluate the work of one or more part-time marketing \ninterns. \n• The position requires travel within assigned territory for 10-12 weeks in a calendar year, \nand the ability to work evenings, partial weekends, and campus visit programs as \nneeded for success. \n• The work requires a valid Texas driver’s license with a favorable driving record. \nBENEFITS  \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions.  \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Baseball%20Coach_08.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "this position will recruit student-athletes that will represent the university in a manner that will",
      "description": " \n \n                                                                                      Job Number: 17118UD \nBaseball Coach                                                Date Posted: August 24, 2026 \n \nWHO WE ARE  \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking a Baseball Coach who will be responsible for the overall operation and \nconduct of the program. The Baseball Coach will provide instruction and guidance to student-\nathletes, demonstrating techniques of the sport in order to prepare them for athletic \ncompetition, analyze student-athlete performance to determine need for individual or team \nimprovement, and schedule and oversee practice sessions and competitive events. Additionally, \nthis position will recruit student-athletes that will represent the university in a manner that will \nreflect favorably upon the university and the athletics department. \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES  \n \n• Organize, prepare, and conduct individual and team practice sessions to train and \nprepare for competition and instruct student-athletes in techniques of the sport. \n• Provide direction, motivation and advice to prepare student-athletes for competitive \nevents; adjust coaching techniques based on student-athlete needs. \n• Apply best practices in athletic conditioning and team training safety. \n• Promote and facilitate student-athlete academic success through a commitment to class \nattendance, academic achievement, and graduation. \n• Establish team and individual student-athlete goals. \n• Ensure player injuries/illnesses are attended to; follow-up with student-athlete and/or \nathletic trainer as needed. \n• Establish and enforce rules and regulations concerning student-athlete conduct, \nappearance, punctuality and other areas deemed appropriate.  \n• Determine competitive event schedule, coordinating with teams as needed. \n• Perform field maintenance, as needed. \n \n• Execute expenditures in accordance with department/university procedures; oversee \nthe purchase of uniforms and equipment.  \n• Arrange transportation to competitive event sites in accordance with university \nprocedures. \n• Coordinate recruitment of student-athletes with Undergraduate Admissions in \naccordance with NCAA rules and regulations through scouting, attending tournaments, \nand home visits. \n• Submit required information to compliance officer. \n• Remain accessible to media and make appearances to promote and/or market program; \nparticipate in fundraising activities. \n• Maintain continual and thorough familiarity with applicable NCAA, Conference, and \nUniversity rules and regulations, ensuring that program, staff and student athletes \noperate within these sets of rules.  \n \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS  \n• Bachelor’s degree. \n• Experience as a player and/or coach in the sport. \n \nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS \n \n• Five to seven years of experience directly related to the duties and responsibilities of \nthe position. \n \nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n \n• May provide general instruction to Assistant Coaches and/or student workers. \n• Must maintain current CPR, AED and First Aid certification. \n• Must participate in Southern Collegiate Athletic Conference groups for the sport.  \nBENEFITS  \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions.  \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Career%20Advisor_07.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "graduates in the job search process. Additionally, this position will market the University to",
      "description": " \n \n                                                                                Job Number: 15348UD \nCareer Advisor                                                                          Date Posted: July 30, 2026 \n \nWHO WE ARE  \n \nThe University of Dallas is a Catholic university that seeks to educate the whole person, \nencouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and primary ends of \neducation. We have consistently ranked as one of the top regional universities in the country. \nWe are dedicated and guided by our Mission. \n \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking a Career Advisor who will guide and coach students and recent \ngraduates in the job search process. Additionally, this position will market the University to \npotential employers and maintain records for those utilizing the Office of Personal Career \nDevelopment (OPCD).  \n \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES  \n \n• Serve as advocate for undergraduate students and recent graduates in the job \nsearch process, including pointed guidance in appropriate career paths and salary \nnegotiations. Develop, track, report, and document employment records for \nstudents/graduates utilizing the OPCD office. \n• Advise, document, and follow-up one-on-one career counseling sessions, including \nconducting practice interviews, critiquing resumes, and developing job search \nstrategies.  \n• Plan and conduct marketing calls and appropriate follow-up with potential \nemployers, which includes educating employers on curriculum offered by \nUniversity and planning and conducting employer visits to campus. \n• Seek employer feedback. Research market trends for various degree programs to aid \nin development of curriculum, assist in the admissions process, and to further educate \nstudents. \n• Maintain student job board (Handshake) to maximize field-related opportunities for \nstudents. \n• Conduct mock interviews and provide resume critiques, including rewrites. \n• Generate creative marketing strategies to promote career services to internal and \nexternal constituents. \n• Assist with research of educational outcomes for all undergraduate students, \nkeeping accurate records.  \n \n \n \n  \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS  \n• Bachelor’s degree in Business, Communications, Psychology, Organizational Behavior, \nHuman Resources, or other with commensurate experience.  \n• One to two years in human resources, corporate recruiting, placement/search firm, \ncareer services or counseling or industry-related position.  \n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.  \n• Superior organizational and problem resolution skills.  \n• Ability to work effectively under pressure and to meet frequently occurring deadlines.  \n \n \n \n \nBENEFITS  \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions.   \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. \n "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Content%20Marketing%20Manager_08.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Job Number: 16838UD",
      "description": " \n \n                                                                                   Job Number: 16838UD \nContent Marketing Manager                                            Date Posted: August 14, 2026 \n \nWHO WE ARE  \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking a Content Marketing Manager who is responsible for developing and \nexecuting strategic communications initiatives that expand awareness of the university’s brand \nand support revenue growth through enrollment and advancement. This role leads media \nrelations efforts, develops compelling written content across multiple platforms, supports \nundergraduate admission marketing communications and manages institutional social media \nand digital content. Success in this role requires exceptional writing, editing, storytelling and \ncontent management skills, including the ability to produce press releases, marketing content, \ndigital content and admission-focused communications that advance the university’s mission \nand strategic priorities. \nThrough digital content creation and management, admission marketing and media relations, \nthe position ensures that university communications consistently reflect these brand attributes \nand strengthen the institution’s connection with prospective students, parents, alumni, donors \nand other key audiences. \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES  \nSocial Media and Digital Content Management \n● Develop and implement content for institutional social media channels that advances \nbrand awareness, engagement and strategic university priorities. \n● Create and edit compelling written content for social media, blogs and other digital \nchannels, ensuring a consistent voice, message and visual identity. \n \n● Develop content that integrates institutional storytelling with enrollment, advancement \nand campus communications priorities. \n● Monitor social media trends, audience engagement and platform performance to \ninform content strategy. \n● Organize, track and manage digital content assets, including copy, images, videos and \nlinks, to support timely publication across social media, web and email channels. \n● Coordinate digital content requests, deadlines and approvals to ensure consistent \nmessaging and efficient workflow. \n● Supervise student interns involved in content creation, social media management and \ndigital communications projects. \nUndergraduate Admission Marketing  \n● Partner with the Office of Undergraduate Admission to develop and implement print, \nemail and digital communications for prospective undergraduate students and families. \n● Write and edit persuasive admission marketing content that communicates the value of \na University of Dallas education and supports recruitment goals. \n● Develop enrollment-focused messaging and storytelling that highlights academic \nexcellence, student outcomes, campus life and the university’s Catholic liberal arts \nmission. \n● Support admission communication campaigns by creating content for brochures, email \nmarketing, web pages and other recruitment materials. \nMedia Relations  \n● Develop and implement public relations strategies to secure earned media coverage \n(local, regional and national) for academic programs, research, faculty expertise, student \nachievements, institutional rankings, events and university initiatives. \n● Cultivate, maintain and deepen relationships with journalists, editors, producers, \nbloggers and other media stakeholders. \n● Monitor news and media trends relevant to higher education, identify opportunities to \ngenerate positive coverage and proactively pitch story ideas. \n● Write and edit press releases, media advisories, feature stories, executive \ncommunications and other public-facing content that advances the university’s visibility \nand reputation. \n \n● Manage publicity surrounding major institutional announcements, events, initiatives \nand accomplishments. \n● Maintain and manage media contact databases and stay current on media best \npractices, emerging outlets and changes in the communications landscape. \n \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS  \n• Bachelor’s degree.  \n• Two (2) or more years of experience in non-profit public relations, marketing, or \nrelated field.  \n• Exceptional writing, editing and proofreading skills, with the ability to communicate \neffectively and persuasively to a variety of audiences. \n• Demonstrated ability to write press releases, feature stories, marketing copy, social \nmedia content and admission-focused communications. \n• Strong storytelling ability and understanding of how to adapt content for media, \nmarketing and recruitment purposes. \n \nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS \n• Hubspot proficiency.  \n• Experience with university administrative databases, such as Slate or Banner. \n• Experience with Modern Campus or a comparable website platform.  \n \nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n \n• This position requires the ability to work evenings, partial weekends and campus visit \nprograms as needed for success.  \n \nBENEFITS  \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions.   \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. \n "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Development%20Project%20Manager_08.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "gifts during campaigns. The Development Project Manager reports to the Assistant Vice",
      "description": " \n \nJob Number: 17138UD \nDevelopment Project Manager Date Posted: August 24, 2026 \n \nWHO WE ARE \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking a Development Project Manager who will be responsible for supporting \nthe implementation of relational giving cycle strategies for development network growth and \ncultivation that fosters long term donor relationships and helps achieve short- and long-term \nfundraising plans through annual restricted and unrestricted support. The Development Project \nManager coordinates the implementation of development projects, executes the distribution of \ncontent for the network, and oversees the distribution of particular engagement to segmented \ndonor groups. This role manages the implementation of student interns’ personalized outreach \nto members of the network, maintains relationships across the university, and directly solicits \ngifts during campaigns. The Development Project Manager reports to the Assistant Vice \nPresident and supports the Development Network Team, particularly with content research, \ncontent distribution, and engagement. This position will apply key principles and best practices \nof higher education advancement, and the role is vital to engaging, retaining, and growing \nnetwork donors. \n \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES \n \n● Development Projects: Manage development network projects to ensure efficient \nproduction, team coordination, and project momentum that delivers both quality and \ntimeliness.  \n● Distribution of Development Content to the Network: Distribute approved content across \ndifferent communication avenues (digital and mail). \n● Distribute Content to Particular Donor Groups: Oversee the distribution of particular \nengagement to segmented donor groups based on a defined cadence for different donor \ngroups (set by the AVP) and attend corresponding donor group events. \n● Oversee Student Intern Outreach: Manage the implementation of student interns’ \npersonalized engagement to members of the network via phone, email, mail, and/or in \nperson events. \n● Maintain Relationships Across the University: Collaborate with faculty, staff, and students \nto gather particular research and information corresponding to development network \n\ncontent projects, build involvement and ownership, and provide a clear line of sight to \nparticular impacts of donor gifts. \n● Directly solicits gifts during campaigns: As part of the Development Network team, \nmembers contact individuals (primarily via phone calls) during campaigns to solicit gifts as \na means to reach the overall campaign fundraising goals. \n● Other duties as assigned to ensure the efficient and effective operation of the \nDevelopment and University Relations Department. \n \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS \n● Bachelor’s degree.  \n● One to three years of development experience.  \n● Superior communication and interpersonal skills, creativity, political astuteness, and tact. \n \nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS \n● Experience working in higher education and/or foundations and sponsored research. \n● Demonstrated previous experience interacting with high-level donors and managing a \nteam of volunteers and/or students. \n● Experience with Slate.  \n \nADDITIONAL INFORMATION    \n \n• Occasional evening or weekend work in support of the Department of Development and \nUniversity Relations.  \n• Manage student workers. \n \nBENEFITS \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions. \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber. \n \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. "
    },
    "https://udallas.edu/offices-services/human-resources/_documents_open_positions/JP_Financial%20Assistant_08.2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Financial Assistant                                              Date Posted: August 06, 2026",
      "description": " \n \n                                                                                   Job Number: 17018UD \nFinancial Assistant                                              Date Posted: August 06, 2026 \n \nWHO WE ARE  \n \nThe University of Dallas is a premier Catholic liberal arts university that seeks to educate the \nwhole person, encouraging its students to pursue wisdom, truth and virtue as the proper and \nprimary ends of education. All employees are expected to support the university’s Mission, \nwhich is informed by the Apostolic Constitution Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Catholic Church’s \ngoverning document on Catholic universities. The University of Dallas is known for its nationally \nranked Core Curriculum, exceptional post-graduation outcomes, and some of the happiest \nstudents in the country. \n \nSUMMARY \n \nUD is currently seeking a Financial Assistant to monitor student accounts, post payments and \ncharges, and take proactive steps to collect accounts receivable. The Financial Assistant will \nprovide excellent customer service and general information to the university community, will \ninvoice third-party billing as well as the oversight of payment plans and payments across a \nnumber of platforms.  This position will demonstrate a high level of attention to detail when \nperforming all tasks. \n \n \nPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES  \n \n• Provide excellent customer service via phone call, email, and in-person to University of \nDallas students and parents answering questions on all facets of student accounts. \n• Post charges and payments for student accounts and miscellaneous transactions from \nvarious platforms. \n• Reconcile cash drawer transactions daily to ensure payments are accounted for and posted \nproperly. \n• Verify accuracy of accounts receivable data, identify and resolve discrepancies. \n• Assist with registration to aid students matriculating in the university. \n• Perform cashiering functions as assigned. \n• Monitor past due accounts and contact students to inquire about payment status according \nto university policies and procedures. \n• Issue account statements. \n• Work with other departments to resolve student-related issues. \n• Process third party billing for students to outside entities, including the Veterans \nAdministration. \n• Oversee assigned projects as needed. \n \n \nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS  \n• Associate’s degree.  \n \nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS \n \n \nADDITIONAL INFORMATION \n \n• Position may require the ability to work evenings and weekends, as necessary.  \n \nBENEFITS  \n \nUD provides competitive pay and benefits, including eligibility to participate in medical, dental, \nvision, life and disability insurance; employee events; a health and wellness program; a free \nfitness center; competitive leave programs; tuition waiver, tuition exchange for employees and \ntheir families; and matching retirement plan contributions.   \n \nIf this sounds like the job for you, apply online at: https://hr.udallas.edu/apply/ \n \n \nThe University of Dallas seeks to recruit, develop, and retain faculty, staff and administration of the highest caliber.  \nThe University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from individuals who will enhance our \ncommunity and advance our Mission. \n "
    },
